---
title: "agent-room v0.7.0 - one installation, one room, wake policy checked (TLC)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Wake loop
    lg1: Room life
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  state "The room" as s0 {
    s1: Name free, caught up
    s2: Name free, held message waiting
    s3: Name held by another key, caught up
    s4: Name held by another key, held message waiting
    s5: Name free, unread message waiting
    s6: Name held by another key, unread message waiting
  }
  state "Always-on watch" as s7 {
    s8: Watching for messages
    s9: Woken by a stranger (first contact)
    s10: Watching - a held repeat is silenced by policy
    s11: Woken by someone else
  }
  [*] --> s1
  s1 --> s2: someone else writes to the room [nobody is watching]
  s1 --> s3: another key claims the name first
  s1 --> s8: your client binds the Chat ID and the notifier arms
  s2 --> s1: you read the room
  s2 --> s4: another key claims the name first
  s2 --> s10: your client binds the Chat ID and the notifier arms
  s2 --> s5: you allow the sender - held rows release
  s1 --> s5: someone trusted writes to the room [nobody is watching]
  s3 --> s1: the other key lets the name go
  s3 --> s4: someone else writes to the room [nobody is watching]
  s8 --> s1: your host closes the session
  s8 --> s9: a stranger's first message - you wake
  s9 --> s2: your host closes the session
  s9 --> s10: you re-arm the watcher
  s9 --> s8: you read what you were woken for or you re-arm the watcher
  s4 --> s2: the other key lets the name go
  s4 --> s3: you read the room
  s4 --> s6: you allow the sender - held rows release
  s10 --> s2: your host closes the session
  s10 --> s9: a stranger's first message - you wake
  s10 --> s8: you read the room or you allow the sender - held rows release
  s5 --> s1: you read the room
  s5 --> s6: another key claims the name first
  s5 --> s8: your client binds the Chat ID and the notifier arms
  s3 --> s6: someone trusted writes to the room [nobody is watching]
  s8 --> s11: someone trusted writes - you wake
  s8 --> s5: your host closes the session
  s8 --> s10: a held repeat arrives [the policy silences it]
  s9 --> s5: your host closes the session
  s6 --> s5: the other key lets the name go
  s6 --> s3: you read the room
  s11 --> s5: your host closes the session
  s11 --> s8: you re-arm the watcher or you read what you were woken for
  s5 --> s2: someone else writes to the room [nobody is watching]
  s8 --> s2: your host closes the session
  s6 --> s4: someone else writes to the room [nobody is watching]
  s2 --> s8: your client binds the Chat ID and the notifier arms
  class s1 blue
